{"step_index":62,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:57:37Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:57:37+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:57:39+02:00\nThe search for \"\"Theorem 2.15\" \"If G is a connected graph of order at least two, then\" \"total domination\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe theorem you are referring to is:\n\n**\"If $G$ is a connected graph of order at least two, then $\\gamma_t(G) \\geq \\text{rad}(G)$.\"**[1][2][3]\n\nThis result is identified as **Theorem 2.15** in the literature on total domination in graphs (specifically cited in works such as those by DeLaVina et al.[1][2]). In this inequality:\n*   $\\gamma_t(G)$ denotes the **total domination number** of the graph $G$[4].\n*   $\\text{rad}(G)$ denotes the **radius** of the graph $G$[2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [scribd.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHOmOG2N8zCsYx0IcvcA8npAru_JysksRcitg5OrzMr9UCew09Iy8gRdD1Y5khNEWuu0mWs4sKH1dEcVA_YvD7pm599IX2ZiiDWiZxDGFkxqHTy5kMvO57D_bep1HkDNOD6HY4MlNyaZjXFsKh-E8eiZrDNIiC3OkIbZQ==)\n[2] [scribd.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHOmOG2N8zCsYx0IcvcA8npAru_JysksRcitg5OrzMr9UCew09Iy8gRdD1Y5khNEWuu0mWs4sKH1dEcVA_YvD7pm599IX2ZiiDWiZxDGFkxqHTy5kMvO57D_bep1HkDNOD6HY4MlNyaZjXFsKh-E8eiZrDNIiC3OkIbZQ==)\n[3] [jomardpublishing.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFt9zxvHwPmBtoCbTsH8_vof5JMz1sUhJrHjyF3FeYWNHZIS4K28x_C0YQqu7FGBOwgGDE5xnvoKPNvKvDdAJGMaQ71QVmV5fC4h5au5egZVTptk2_0kHTTCnAt9RoRUBqhVCOQGnFw1F2LOvMzgd5M8UwZl9k175PhMMDpw69WFBx9c0xzXv8=)\n[4] [bibliotekanauki.pl](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGGuMS70IiVOSMKOoclV1l2eCpyZBRHjzMmmxtodB3ehdenrCrI9XsDKAAGDLOX7OqksR8AU-PONmOD7yci4KmZcw_fhnmo6HStVkl4AJLiZahAsM79iUdhf3Jge6Q2r_Ye3gXWg1A=)"}
